---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import provenance from '../data/_provenance.json';

// Generated from src/data/_provenance.json so the table cannot drift from the manifest
// the data tooling reads.
const LEVEL_ORDER = ['sourced', 'derived', 'ai_authored', 'observed', 'config'];
const used = new Set();
for (const fields of Object.values(provenance.datasets ?? {})) {
  if (fields && typeof fields === 'object') {
    for (const v of Object.values(fields)) if (typeof v === 'string') used.add(v);
  }
}
const levels = LEVEL_ORDER
  .filter((k) => used.has(k) && provenance.levels?.[k])
  .map((k) => ({ label: k.replace(/_/g, ' '), desc: provenance.levels[k] }));

const sources = provenance.primary_sources ?? [];
const updated = (provenance.updated_at ?? '').slice(0, 10);
---

<Base
  title="How This Site Is Made — ClinicFinder"
  description="How ClinicFinder is built: facility data comes from OpenStreetMap open data, what that means for accuracy and coverage, who is responsible, and how to report a wrong address."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>How This Site Is Made</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Where the facility information comes from, what it does and does not cover, and how
      to tell us when something is wrong.
    </p>

    <h2>The written content is AI-drafted and human-supervised</h2>
    <p>
      The explanatory text on this site — what a clinic type does, what to expect at a
      facility, how to prepare for a visit — is drafted by AI and reviewed by a person.
      The facility records themselves are not written by AI: they come from open data, as
      set out below.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible for it</h2>
    <p>
      Editorial responsibility for ClinicFinder is held by the site's operator, a real
      person who reviews what is published here and answers the contact address below. AI
      drafts the explanatory text; it does not decide unsupervised what gets published,
      and it is not the party accountable for it.
    </p>

    {sources.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <h2>Where the facility data comes from</h2>
        <ul>
          {sources.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>What is sourced, and what is written</h2>
    <p>
      Every field carries a provenance class. These are the classes actually in use, taken
      from the manifest this site is built from:
    </p>
    <dl class="provenance-list">
      {levels.map((l) => (
        <div class="provenance-row">
          <dt><code>{l.label}</code></dt>
          <dd>{l.desc}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <p>
      Facility names, addresses and coordinates are <strong>sourced</strong> — they are
      not estimated, and they are not adjusted by us. We do not rewrite a facility's name
      even when it is obviously misspelled, because changing a sourced value while it
      still reads as sourced is its own kind of error.
    </p>

    <h2>The honest caveat: coverage, not invention</h2>
    <p>
      The limitation here is not that figures are made up — it is that OpenStreetMap is
      community-maintained, so how complete and how current the data is varies a great
      deal by area. A well-mapped city may have every facility with phone numbers and
      opening hours; a rural district may have a handful of pins and nothing else. Each
      facility page shows a data-quality indicator and when the record was last checked,
      so you can see which one you are looking at.
    </p>
    <p>
      This matters more here than on an ordinary comparison site. A wrong address costs
      someone a trip they may not be able to afford. <strong>Please phone ahead before
      travelling</strong>, especially to a facility whose record looks sparse, and treat
      opening hours as a starting point rather than a guarantee.
    </p>

    <h2>Found something wrong? Please tell us</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections are genuinely welcome and they help everyone who looks up the same
      facility after you. Email
      <a href="mailto:hello@clinicfinder.co.za">hello@clinicfinder.co.za</a> or use the
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a> with the facility name and what is wrong —
      a changed phone number, a closed facility, a wrong location — and it will be
      checked and corrected.
    </p>

    <p class="meta">Provenance manifest last updated: {updated}</p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .lead { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    h2 { margin-top: 2rem; }
    p, li { line-height: 1.7; }
    .meta { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.7; }
    .provenance-list { margin: 1.25rem 0; }
    .provenance-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 0.7rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.25);
    }
    .provenance-row dt code { font-size: 0.85rem; white-space: nowrap; }
    .provenance-row dd { margin: 0; line-height: 1.6; }
    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .provenance-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.25rem; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
